  "title": "Commit-message gate rules reach the commit scan",
  "summary": "Adds a structural commit-message rule set to the writing lint: a new `commit-subject-missing` detector, a `COMMIT_GATE_RULES` list (subject present, no bare reference, reference carries a label), and a `commit_gate_findings` helper. The `commit-msg` hook already ran the writing lint in commit context, so it picks the new rule up for free; the real change is that both commit-scan paths (`osf scan --commits` and `osf check scan-commits`) now chain those gate findings onto the scan rules, so a bad subject or bare reference fails the pre-push checkpoint and the pull request check, not just the local hook. Docs and CONTRIBUTING are updated to say which rules are structural and which are not checked at all.",
